      en: "The Sauka Ancient Mound, located in the heart of the Selonian Highlands, is one of the most significant archaeological sites in southern Latvia. This prehistoric hillfort served for centuries as a fortified center for local Baltic tribes, particularly the Selonians. Its strategic position on a natural elevation provided a commanding view over Lake Sauka, the largest lake in the region, allowing for effective defense against potential invaders. Archaeological excavations have revealed settlement layers dating back to the 1st millennium BC, providing valuable insights into the social structures and craftsmanship of the early inhabitants. The site is shrouded in local folklore, with legends speaking of sunken castles and ancient deities, highlighting its historical and spiritual importance. In 1987, the area was incorporated into the Sauka Nature Park to protect both its cultural heritage and unique biodiversity. Today, visitors encounter a peaceful landscape characterized by rolling hills and dense mixed forests. The mound remains a vital symbol of regional identity and a key destination for those exploring the historical landscape of Selonia.",
